{"parentUuid":"53ab50ea-4293-4b90-bd1e-fc3333e55866","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01UHa1PpYz7k78vpviXoRxpa","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"03a2a316-cc35-42d5-afdf-6c5ba93d68ae","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:05:26.060Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\hp\\NetCortex","sessionId":"88958964-2992-40b7-a2b1-a4d7674680fc","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"a/ui","slug":"wiggly-plotting-biscuit"}
{"parentUuid":"03a2a316-cc35-42d5-afdf-6c5ba93d68ae","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAP89JCeWzpKCH6kMW5Z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Step 1 is done and `main` is pushed. Your message cut off after \"Simulate incident\":, so I built the dashboard from my best guess at the rest. It's on its own branch and running at http://localhost:8000/.\n\n## Step 1: main\n\n- **a/demo-hardening:** you had already merged PR #10. I merged the one commit after it (the e2e wait fix), ran the tests and pushed `main`.\n- **Partner branch:** it was already in `main` (PR #1), so I only checked it:\n  - `uv sync --all-packages` works, 275 tests pass and `ruff check` is clean.\n  - The trigger is still our rule-based detector, and TabPFN stays off until it's configured.\n  - `sim-tower` still uses our stand-in, even though his simulator now knows that site too. His other sites (such as `north-tower`) go to his simulator.\n  - His merge changed nothing in our folders.\n- **apps/web:** deleted and pushed (`84d6bd5`). Two leftovers point at it:\n  - CI's web job now skips itself.\n  - `infra/render/render.yaml` would fail to deploy the web service.\n\n  Say if you want both cleaned up.\n- The two background e2e runs are stopped; the first was mid-run.\n\n## Step 2: dashboard (branch `a/ui`, not merged)\n\nhttps://github.com/aunraza19/NetCortex/compare/main...a/ui?expand=1\n\nIt's three files in `services/api/src/netcortex_api/ui/` (HTML, CSS, plain JS) and loads nothing external. I checked it in headless Chrome at 1280 px (light and dark) and at 390 px. 276 tests pass, including a new one for `/`.\n\n- **Top bar:** NetCortex, then each site with its status (OK, DEGRADED, DOWN or NO DATA) and latency. The latency is the site's worst current round-trip time, since that's what the API reports. A LIVE / RECONNECTING indicator sits on the right.\n- **Simulate incident:** site, scenario (heavy user, uplink down, slow DNS) and duration, then Inject.\n- **Incidents:** status label, cause, site and time. The newest is selected automatically, and a newly opened incident takes over the selection when it appears. Phones show the latest 8.\n- **Incident detail:**\n  - status, summary, diagnosis (agent and detector) and evidence;\n  - a chart of the key metric with the opening time marked;\n  - router commands and rollback in monospace;\n  - the CHR dry-run result with its failure reason;\n  - Approve and Reject buttons while the incident awaits approval;\n  - customer messages in English and Urdu (right-to-left);\n  - the timeline.\n- **Live updates:** the page refreshes from the existing event stream.\n- **Look:** black, white and grays only, system fonts, 1 px lines. There are no shadows, gradients, icons or emoji. Dark mode follows the system setting.\n- **Safety:** text from the API is always inserted as text, never as HTML.\n\nI dropped the forecast band from the chart: the stand-in detector's overlapping forecasts drew as spiky gray shapes.\n\nThe worker and the API are running on `a/ui`, and CHR is the freshly reset instance.\n\nPaste the rest of your step 2 spec and I'll adjust, or tell me to merge `a/ui` into `main` as it is."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":645,"cache_read_input_tokens":387764,"output_tokens":1122,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":645,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1122,"cache_read_input_tokens":387764,"cache_creation_input_tokens":645,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":645},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"4b97fea2-5005-4371-814d-8fd58ef989e3","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgAP88pBy4koxtmm9sRaq","requestRef":"c7be7305-a591-4e02-8f36-c6746be8349e","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"1d166d54-79dd-40bd-ac64-b25ab6c15494","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:05:26.058Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\hp\\NetCortex","sessionId":"88958964-2992-40b7-a2b1-a4d7674680fc","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"a/ui","slug":"wiggly-plotting-biscuit"}
