{"parentUuid":"1882d14c-f779-4a98-b2a0-8aad07d9299e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"8ad07978-83e5-4119-af66-713ca2474a9c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I tested a/ui end to end: <it worked / these issues: \nMake the post-apply watch time a setting (default 300 s). For demo recording I'll set it\nto 60 s. Also show \"Watching results, verdict at HH:MM\" in the UI while verifying, so it\ndoesn't look stuck..\n\n1. Fix any issues above, then merge a/ui into main. Also delete infra/render/render.yaml\n   and the web CI job (we're local-demo only). Push main.\n\n2. Honesty audit before the post. List each partner technology and whether it is LIVE in\n   the demo, STUBBED or NOT USED, with evidence: Gemma 4 (agent), EmbeddingGemma +\n   pgvector runbook search (is the index built? does search_runbook return real chunks?),\n   TabPFN second opinion (has it ever answered a real incident?), Temporal, Sentry\n   (gen_ai spans), Tiger Data (TimescaleDB hypertables), SerpApi check_news (is there a\n   key? real or stub?), Entire (checkpoints on our commits?), GitHub Actions.\n   Also list what I would need to do to turn on the stubbed ones, and how long each\n   would take.\n\n3. Draft the DEV post in docs/post/post.md (Markdown, written for humans; writing quality\n   is judged most). Use only facts from this repo, PR descriptions, Sentry traces and our\n   runs; claim only what the audit marks LIVE. Structure:\n   - Title + one-line hook\n   - What NetCortex is and who would pay (small ISPs / gaming cafes, evening complaints)\n   - Demo: [VIDEO PLACEHOLDER] + where screenshots go\n   - How it works: architecture (collector -> TimescaleDB -> rule trigger -> Temporal\n     incident workflow -> Gemma agent with tools -> template-only fixes -> CHR dry run ->\n     human approval -> apply -> verify -> auto-rollback)\n   - Safety design: template-only commands, param validation, CHR dry run, nc-<id> naming,\n     never touching pre-existing config, approval, auto-rollback (tell the real rollback\n     story from trace 5837ffbb...)\n   - Why open models: local Gemma on a Mac mini, privacy, offline, cost; the thinking\n     on/off table (9.0 s vs 33.6 s, accuracy) and the 10/11 reliability result\n   - Data: live collector from a home connection in Pakistan (7 targets incl. a Dubai\n     game server), the 8.8.8.8 vs 1.1.1.1 DNS finding, plus whatever of the partner's\n     RIPE Atlas / simulator work is real\n   - Observability with Sentry: traces, gen_ai spans with token counts, links\n   - Results table (the e2e runs)\n   - Honest limits (simulated incidents, CHR carries no real traffic, TabPFN status,\n     TabPFN-3.5 non-commercial licence if used)\n   - What's next\n   - Built with: partner tech list (LIVE ones only), team: Aun + partner\n   Keep sentences short and plain. Push it.\n\n\n\nalso truthfuly list every partner terch we used correctly."}]},"uuid":"4ce32324-acc8-4413-913f-9f9f95e2f1b1","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:21:24.279Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"human"},"promptSource":"sdk","turnOrigin":"human","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":18,"turnIndex":25},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\hp\\NetCortex","sessionId":"88958964-2992-40b7-a2b1-a4d7674680fc","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"a/ui","slug":"wiggly-plotting-biscuit"}
