{"parentUuid":"a5631780-698a-4868-b5df-6307d829cf86","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"8ad07978-83e5-4119-af66-713ca2474a9c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NeKV7UVzMiuL8Gso5s4nQS","type":"tool_result","content":"# Post research notes\n\nKeep only findings backed by a source, a reproducible run, or a clearly labeled team observation. Record the date, method, and limits with each result. Do not invent performance numbers, customer feedback, first users, or claims that the hosted demo is live.\n\n## Evidence log\n\n- 2026-10-18: Build plan identifies small WISPs, gaming cafes, and freelance network engineers as intended users. This is a target audience, not evidence of a customer interview or first user.\n- 2026-10-18: The planned hosted demo uses replayed/simulated data. Any published demo must label that data clearly.\n- Pending: measured detector evaluation, model/runtime details, real baseline provenance, first-user feedback, and hosted demo URL/status.\n\n## Draft post outline\n\nNetCortex is being built for small network operators who need an affordable way to spot deteriorating links and review a tested RouterOS fix. The intended flow collects or replays network metrics, detects unusual behavior, explains the evidence, tests a constrained fix on a virtual router, and waits for a human decision.\n\nOpen-weight local inference is intended to keep network context on-site, support diagnosis during internet outages, and avoid per-token charges for the core workflow. These are design goals; claims about measured privacy, reliability, cost, or accuracy require implementation and evidence.\n\nThe hosted demo is planned to use simulated/replayed telemetry. TabPFN cloud sends anonymized metrics to its provider and its current license terms may restrict commercial use; verify the applicable terms before making product claims. Cloud outage-search integrations are optional and may require paid credentials.\n\nBefore publication, replace this draft with verified implementation details, evaluation results, limitations, a working demo link if available, and an actual first-user account only if one exists and consents to being described.\n': ['1.1.1.1', '8.8.8.8']} summary='The current DNS resolver is experiencing high latency and packet loss. Switching to a different resolver should resolve the issue.'\\n\\nthinking off: median 9.0s, cause 6/6, template 5/6, params 5/6, retries 1, fallbacks 1, avg tool calls 4.3\\nthinking on : median 33.6s, cause 4/6, template 3/6, params 3/6, retries 2, fallbacks 1, avg tool calls 4.8\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"uuid\":\"21fdb3ae-b4d2-4b81-90ae-e78123dde815\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-18T16:23:42.367Z\",\"toolUseResult\":{\"stdout\":\"thinking=off heavy_user   run1    9.6s cause=Y template=queue_limit     params=Y too\n': ['1.1.1.1', '8.8.8.8']} summary='The current DNS resolver is experiencing high latency and packet loss. Switching to a different resolver should resolve the issue.'\\n\\nthinking off: median 9.0s, cause 6/6, template 5/6, params 5/6, retries 1, fallbacks 1, avg tool calls 4.3\\nthinking on : median 33.6s, cause 4/6, template 3/6, params 3/6, retries 2, fallbacks 1, avg tool calls 4.8\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false},\"serverClassifierContext\":{\"request\":\"df168934-86a6-4d75-aa6d-baaf8d5cdd48\",\"context\":{\"git_state\":{\"cwd\":\"/c/Users/hp/NetCortex\",\"root\":\"/c/U","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"673649d3-5eb1-43bf-aac9-18505a686315","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:27:46.135Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# Post research notes\n\nKeep only findings backed by a source, a reproducible run, or a clearly labeled team observation. Record the date, method, and limits with each result. Do not invent performance numbers, customer feedback, first users, or claims that the hosted demo is live.\n\n## Evidence log\n\n- 2026-10-18: Build plan identifies small WISPs, gaming cafes, and freelance network engineers as intended users. This is a target audience, not evidence of a customer interview or first user.\n- 2026-10-18: The planned hosted demo uses replayed/simulated data. Any published demo must label that data clearly.\n- Pending: measured detector evaluation, model/runtime details, real baseline provenance, first-user feedback, and hosted demo URL/status.\n\n## Draft post outline\n\nNetCortex is being built for small network operators who need an affordable way to spot deteriorating links and review a tested RouterOS fix. The intended flow collects or replays network metrics, detects unusual behavior, explains the evidence, tests a constrained fix on a virtual router, and waits for a human decision.\n\nOpen-weight local inference is intended to keep network context on-site, support diagnosis during internet outages, and avoid per-token charges for the core workflow. These are design goals; claims about measured privacy, reliability, cost, or accuracy require implementation and evidence.\n\nThe hosted demo is planned to use simulated/replayed telemetry. TabPFN cloud sends anonymized metrics to its provider and its current license terms may restrict commercial use; verify the applicable terms before making product claims. Cloud outage-search integrations are optional and may require paid credentials.\n\nBefore publication, replace this draft with verified implementation details, evaluation results, limitations, a working demo link if available, and an actual first-user account only if one exists and consents to being described.\n': ['1.1.1.1', '8.8.8.8']} summary='The current DNS resolver is experiencing high latency and packet loss. Switching to a different resolver should resolve the issue.'\\n\\nthinking off: median 9.0s, cause 6/6, template 5/6, params 5/6, retries 1, fallbacks 1, avg tool calls 4.3\\nthinking on : median 33.6s, cause 4/6, template 3/6, params 3/6, retries 2, fallbacks 1, avg tool calls 4.8\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"uuid\":\"21fdb3ae-b4d2-4b81-90ae-