{"parentUuid":"e80a8d26-6b24-4c72-a829-9f03f004dc48","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgARCMPKp4BHRZDUuSmBk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":532,"cache_read_input_tokens":457674,"output_tokens":1731,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":307},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":532,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1731,"cache_read_input_tokens":457674,"cache_creation_input_tokens":532,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":532},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":10671,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"4b45e38b-86ee-4394-b481-ec49f8df449f","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgARCLvYDtqTrSak78bod","requestRef":"18124975-8e3e-42e6-8b9e-39c1e1690987","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c5f6363d-2e83-4be7-a132-8075e99a7be6","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:32:37.838Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\hp\\NetCortex","sessionId":"88958964-2992-40b7-a2b1-a4d7674680fc","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"merge-main","slug":"wiggly-plotting-biscuit"}
{"parentUuid":"c5f6363d-2e83-4be7-a132-8075e99a7be6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgARCMPKp4BHRZDUuSmBk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Parts 1 and 3 are pushed and part 2 is below. One check is still running in the background: a second heavy_user run without resetting CHR, so the first run's queue is still on the router. I'll report it when it finishes.\n\n## 1. Fixes, merged and pushed (`main` at `bbde638`)\n\n- **Watch time:** `VERIFY_WAIT_S` was already a setting (default 300 s), but running monitors kept their old value. They now restart when the worker starts, so a new value takes effect.\n- **Short watches:** the verdict now compares only the time since the fix. With a 60 s watch, the old code also counted data from before the fix.\n- **Dashboard:** while verifying it shows \"Watching results, verdict at HH:MM\".\n- **Scenario duration:** the dashboard default is now 2 minutes. The simulated recovery only starts when the scenario ends, so a 5-minute scenario would still be running at a 60 s verdict, and the fix would roll back.\n- **Tested with a 60 s watch:** heavy_user opened at 77 s, was approved, and resolved 62 s after the watch began (52.1 → 32.1 ms).\n- **Removed:** `infra/render/` and the web CI job.\n- **Tests:** 277 pass and `ruff check` is clean.\n\nThe worker is running with `VERIFY_WAIT_S=60` set only for this process. For recording, put `VERIFY_WAIT_S=60` in `.env`, restart the worker, and approve promptly.\n\n## 2. Partner technology audit (full evidence in `docs/post/audit.md`)\n\n**Used, and doing real work in the demo (LIVE):**\n- **Gemma 4 E4B:** writes every incident report; 10 of 11 runs gave a valid report with the right template; its calls show up in Sentry with token counts.\n- **Temporal:** monitor and incident workflows, and approval as a signal; 25 workflow runs so far.\n- **Sentry:** one trace per incident, including the model-call spans and the real rollback.\n- **Tiger Data:** TimescaleDB hypertables; 12,478 rows from the live collector plus the simulated site.\n- **GitHub Actions:** 61 runs. CI boots CHR on GitHub's machine and tests every fix template; the latest runs passed.\n- **Entire:** 42 checkpoints, all on your commits. The partner's Codex commits have none.\n\n**Wired in but returning nothing (STUBBED):**\n- **EmbeddingGemma + pgvector runbook search:** the index table is empty (0 rows), so search returns `[]`.\n  - To turn on: run the partner's `runbook ingest`. About 20–40 minutes; it has never been run before.\n- **SerpApi news check:** no API key is set, so it reports \"unavailable\".\n  - To turn on: create a free account and put the key in `.env`. About 5–10 minutes.\n\n**Not used (NOT USED):**\n- **TabPFN:** never answered a real incident. Its only run was the partner's cloud test, which guessed the wrong cause and took 115 s per detection.\n  - To turn on: 45–90 minutes and high risk, so I'd leave it for after the deadline.\n- **Render, .tech domain, Tinker, ElevenLabs:** not used.\n\n## 3. Post: `docs/post/post.md`\n\nIt follows your structure and claims only the LIVE items. Every number comes from our runs, the database or Sentry. Points to check before publishing:\n- **DNS finding:** lookups through 8.8.8.8 take 34.1 ms at the median against 11.2 ms through 1.1.1.1. That's three times slower on your connection, and the ping gap is similar.\n- **Rollback story:** told as it happened: our detector was wrong, the dry run passed, the fix was applied, there was no improvement, and it rolled itself back.\n- **Approvals:** the post says the test script pressed Approve in the end-to-end runs.\n- **Partner's name:** I used \"Muhammad Anas Muqeem\", taken from his git author name. Please confirm it, and add DEV handles.\n- **Placeholders:** the video and three screenshots are marked in the text.\n- **Sentry links:** they need a Sentry login, and the post says so; the screenshots carry that part."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":532,"cache_read_input_tokens":457674,"output_tokens":1731,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":307},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":532,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1731,"cache_read_input_tokens":457674,"cache_creation_input_tokens":532,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":532},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"4b45e38b-86ee-4394-b481-ec49f8df449f","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgARCLvYDtqTrSak78bod","requestRef":"18124975-8e3e-42e6-8b9e-39c1e1690987","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"63ac5f56-015b-4bd1-9f2b-49104b5265ba","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:32:43.330Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\hp\\NetCortex","sessionId":"88958964-2992-40b7-a2b1-a4d7674680fc","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"merge-main","slug":"wiggly-plotting-biscuit"}
