{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"88958964-2992-40b7-a2b1-a4d7674680fc","hash":"ee0bcce4f83b4d3eb389b10d5d526dc53da119f5ad70f4b756381e6df81d7814","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The second run didn't exercise the fix. The incident opened only at 276 s, held back by the 4-minute cooldown after the previous heavy_user incident. By then the 2-minute scenario was over, so the subscriber's rate was back to normal and no valid cap existed. Gemma's proposals failed validation twice and it fell back to notify-only (`none`), which is the safe outcome.\n\nSo with short scenarios, wait until the cooldown has passed before repeating the same scenario. I'll run it once more the right way: wait out the cooldown, then inject. That gives a real check that a second fix applies without resetting CHR."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MfCZUWKUKqTPEqFtQZ9gc5","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/hp/NetCortex && uv run python -c \"\nimport json, time, urllib.request\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone, timedelta\ninc = [i for i in json.load(urllib.request.urlopen('http://127.0.0.1:8000/incidents')) if i['site_id']=='sim-tower' and i['cause']=='heavy_user'][0]\nready = datetime.fromisoformat(inc['closed_at']) + timedelta(minutes=4, seconds=20)\nwait = (ready - datetime.now(timezone.utc)).total_seconds()\nprint('last heavy_user', inc['id'][:8], 'closed', inc['closed_at'][11:19], '; waiting', max(0, round(wait)), 's for the cooldown', flush=True)\ntime.sleep(max(0, wait))\n\" && uv run python infra/scripts/e2e.py heavy_user --duration 2 2>&1 | grep -v 'summary:' | tail -18","description":"Wait out cooldown, then rerun heavy_user without CHR reset","run_in_background":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
