{"parentUuid":"74d93a68-1cf9-46a1-82fc-4fa8e21aac04","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgARoNGt9ugtqMyN3mLjF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The router part now works without resetting CHR. The first fix (`nc-a004c369`) was still on the router, and the second (`nc-f83a14a0-limit-10.0.0.42`) passed its dry run and applied with no name clash.\n\nBut the incident rolled back, and that matters for your recording:\n\n| Step | Time after inject |\n|---|---|\n| Incident opened | 33 s (fast this time) |\n| Approved | 51 s |\n| Fix applied | about 57 s |\n| Verdict (60 s watch) | about 117 s |\n| 2-minute scenario ends | 120 s |\n\nThe whole watch fell inside the simulated incident, so latency went 36.3 → 89.5 ms and the rollback was correct behaviour. The underlying problem: the simulated recovery starts when the scenario's duration runs out, not when the fix is applied. Whether a run resolves therefore depends on how fast the incident opens and how fast you click Approve. Earlier, the 19fc run hit the opposite edge: it opened after the scenario had ended, and Gemma found no valid fix.\n\nTwo ways to make the recording reliable:\n\n1. **Recover when the fix is applied (I recommend this; about 20 minutes).** On the simulated `sim-tower` only, applying a fix replaces the rest of the scripted incident with normal data from that moment. Every approved fix then resolves, whatever the timing. The post already says the recovery is scripted, so it stays honest; I'd add one sentence saying the scripted recovery starts when the fix is applied.\n2. **No code; a recording recipe.** Use a 3-minute scenario with the 300 s watch. In the earlier runs, 5-minute scenarios resolved every time, and a 3-minute one ends before any verdict window opens. Videos would need cutting around the wait, and the timing could still slip.\n\nWant me to do option 1?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":703,"cache_read_input_tokens":463259,"output_tokens":2202,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1587},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":703,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2202,"cache_read_input_tokens":463259,"cache_creation_input_tokens":703,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":703},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"c771ae80-acf4-4c95-855a-89c3c2e6b645","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgARoMv3qkXXWZMUwoRLc","requestRef":"13dd3b2d-40dc-4c9d-a892-362a5a3f4b41","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"6873bdbc-74b1-4748-9b8f-535934fd8bab","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:40:45.945Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\hp\\NetCortex","sessionId":"88958964-2992-40b7-a2b1-a4d7674680fc","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"merge-main","slug":"wiggly-plotting-biscuit"}
