{"parentUuid":"90aba3ab-e003-4b62-ba27-9d7bbd1301af","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d4b1eb7e-fd38-4b94-9280-993e91f797a6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\n<pasted_content id=\"5505\">\nWe're wrapping up for a clean local demo. Do all of this, then push main.\n\n1. Strip non-working features from the RUNNING system (don't delete the partner's\n   packages; they stay as unused experimental code):\n   - Agent: remove the search_runbook and check_news tools. Remove upstream_check from\n     what the model produces (keep the schema field only if removing it is risky;\n     then always null and hidden).\n   - Workflow: remove the TabPFN second-opinion step and the DETECTOR_ARTIFACT startup\n     hook. The rule-based detector is the only detector.\n   - UI: remove the \"second opinion\" and \"upstream check\" sections.\n   - Update tests; remove dead stubs. Keep CHR, Gemma, Temporal, Sentry and Tiger\n     untouched.\n2. Make VERIFY_WAIT_S default to 60 for the demo (a note in .env.example says production\n   uses 300).\n3. Add infra/scripts/start-demo.ps1: opens separate windows for the Temporal dev server\n   (var/temporal.db), CHR start, worker, API and collector (from ../NetCortex-run), skips\n   any already running (check ports 7233, 9180, 8000), then runs check_ollama.py and\n   prints the dashboard URL. Plus stop-demo.ps1. Document both in README.md\n   (\"Run the demo\").\n4. Restart the worker and API on the new code. Run heavy_user, uplink_down and dns_slow\n   end to end once each (wait out cooldowns; different causes don't need to wait).\n   Report the results.\n5. Update docs/post/post.md:\n   - Remove all mentions of SerpApi, runbook search, EmbeddingGemma, pgvector and the\n     TabPFN second opinion as features. In \"Honest limits\" / \"What's next\", one line:\n     \"We built TabPFN forecasting and docs search but cut them before the deadline;\n     they weren't reliable enough.\"\n   - Check \"home internet gets slow in the evening\" against our collector data (median\n     and p95 RTT to 1.1.1.1 and 8.8.8.8, evening 19:00-01:00 PKT vs other hours). Use the\n     numbers if they support it; otherwise soften. Show me the numbers.\n   - Add a short \"Where open beat closed\" paragraph: a cloud LLM API would see subscriber\n     IPs, traffic and router config, would be unreachable during the uplink outage it is\n     meant to diagnose, and bills per token. Say we did not benchmark a closed model.\n   - Add the results of today's runs from step 4. Tighten the post by ~15% without\n     losing numbers. Built with: Gemma 4, Temporal, Sentry, Tiger Data, GitHub Actions,\n     Entire.\n   - Entire: give me 2 checkpoint session links to include (the agent build, and the\n     fix-rollback bug), or tell me if they aren't public.\n6. Final check: tests and ruff pass, git status is clean, main is pushed. Give me a\n   short \"how to run the demo\" summary.\n</pasted_content id=\"5505\">\n"}]},"uuid":"68072c3c-989c-4489-b519-03057d375466","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:41:21.172Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"human"},"promptSource":"sdk","turnOrigin":"human","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":19,"turnIndex":28},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\hp\\NetCortex","sessionId":"88958964-2992-40b7-a2b1-a4d7674680fc","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"merge-main","slug":"wiggly-plotting-biscuit"}
