{"parentUuid":"e849dbdc-c60f-418b-b714-1e4758606c79","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d4b1eb7e-fd38-4b94-9280-993e91f797a6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TTKZ4EGNksGpr8os17WUDV","type":"tool_result","content":"The file C:\\Users\\hp\\NetCortex\\README.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"ba55309b-3ebf-4a2e-b6f5-ee67c9e02566","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:48:12.388Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"update","filePath":"C:\\Users\\hp\\NetCortex\\README.md","content":"# NetCortex\n\nAn on-call network engineer for small ISPs and gaming cafés that runs on local hardware.\nIt watches a site, opens an incident when something goes wrong, has a local Gemma model\nexplain the likely cause and pick one fix from tested MikroTik templates, dry-runs that fix\non a virtual router, waits for a person to approve it, applies it, and rolls it back if the\nkey metric doesn't improve.\n\n```\ncollector -> TimescaleDB -> rule-based detector -> Temporal incident workflow\n  -> Gemma agent (tools) -> template-only fix -> CHR dry run -> human approval\n  -> apply -> watch -> verify -> resolved, or automatic rollback\n```\n\n## Run the demo\n\nNeeds: Windows, [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/), the Temporal CLI, QEMU (for the CHR test\nrouter), Ollama with `gemma4:e4b` reachable at `OLLAMA_BASE_URL`, and a `.env` made from\n[.env.example](.env.example) (Tiger Cloud `DATABASE_URL`, `CHR_PASSWORD`, optional\n`SENTRY_DSN_BACKEND`).\n\n```powershell\nuv sync\npowershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File infra\\scripts\\start-demo.ps1\n```\n\n[start-demo.ps1](infra/scripts/start-demo.ps1) opens a window each for the Temporal dev\nserver (`var/temporal.db`, UI on :8233), the CHR test router (REST on :9180), the worker,\nthe API and the live collector (from `..\\NetCortex-run`, a second checkout). Anything\nalready running is left alone. It then checks the model server and prints the dashboard\nURL: **http://localhost:8000/**\n\nIn the dashboard, pick a scenario under \"Simulate incident\" (heavy user, uplink down, slow\nDNS) and press Inject. Within a minute or two an incident opens with Gemma's report, the\nrouter commands and the CHR dry-run result. Approve it after the scenario ends (the note\nunder Inject gives the time): the simulated site recovers then, and the fix is judged\nafter a 60-second watch (`VERIFY_WAIT_S`; production would use 300). The same scenario\ncan run again 4 minutes after its last incident closes.\n\nTo stop everything:\n\n```powershell\npowershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File infra\\scripts\\stop-demo.ps1            # all of it\npowershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File infra\\scripts\\stop-demo.ps1 -KeepCollector\n```\n\nFrom a terminal instead of the dashboard: `uv run python infra/scripts/e2e.py heavy_user`\ninjects, waits, approves and prints the timeline.\n\n## Layout\n\n| Path | What it is |\n|---|---|\n| `packages/core` | Shared schemas, settings, database helpers, migrations |\n| `packages/agent` | The Pydantic AI agent on Gemma, the rule-based detector, the scenario injector |\n| `packages/fixes` | Fix templates' validation, rendering, CHR dry run, apply and rollback |\n| `templates/routeros` | The four fix templates (YAML) |\n| `services/worker` | Temporal workflows and activities, Sentry tracing |\n| `services/api` | FastAPI: REST, server-sent events, approvals, and the dashboard at `/` |\n| `services/collector` | Live pings and DNS timings from a real connection |\n| `infra/chr` | The MikroTik CHR test router in QEMU, and the template test harness |\n| `packages/detector`, `simgen`, `runbook`, `notify`, `eval`, `data` | The partner's experimental TabPFN detector, simulator, docs search and news check; not used by the running system |\n\nTests: `uv sync --all-packages`, then `uv run pytest -m \"not live\"` and `uv run ruff check .`\n\nMIT licence.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":1,"newStart":1,"newLines":66,"lines":["-## HI","\\ No newline at end of file","+# NetCortex","+","+An on-call network engineer for small ISPs and gaming cafés that runs on local hardware.","+It watches a site, opens an incident when something goes wrong, has a local Gemma model","+explain the likely cause and pick one fix from tested MikroTik templates, dry-runs that fix","+on a virtual router, waits for a person to approve it, applies it, and rolls it back if the","+key metric doesn't improve.","+","+```","+collector -> TimescaleDB -> rule-based detector -> Temporal incident workflow","+  -> Gemma agent (tools) -> template-only fix -> CHR dry run -> human approval","+  -> apply -> watch -> verify -> resolved, or automatic rollback","+```","+","+## Run the demo","+","+Needs: Windows, [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/), the Temporal CLI, QEMU (for the CHR test","+router), Ollama with `gemma4:e4b` reachable at `OLLAMA_BASE_URL`, and a `.env` made from","+[.env.example](.env.example) (Tiger Cloud `DATABASE_URL`, `CHR_PASSWORD`, optional","+`SENTRY_DSN_BACKEND`).","+","+```powershell","+uv sync","+powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File infra\\scripts\\start-demo.ps1","+```","+","+[start-demo.ps1](infra/scripts/start-demo.ps1) opens a window each for the Temporal dev","+server (`var/temporal.db`, UI on :8233), the CHR test router (REST on :9180), the worker,","+the API and the live collector (from `..\\NetCortex-run`, a second checkout). Anything","+already running is left alone. It then checks the model server and prints the dashboard","+URL: **http://localhost:8000/**","+","+In the dashboard, pick a scenario under \"Simulate incident\" (heavy user, uplink down, slow","+DNS) and press Inject. Within a minute or two an incident opens with Gemma's report, the","+router commands and the CHR dry-run result. Approve it after the scenario ends (the note","+under Inject gives the time): the simulated site recovers then, and the fix is judged","+after a 60-second watch (`VERIFY_WAIT_S`; production would use 300). The same scenario","+can run again 4 minutes after its last incident closes.","+","+To stop everything:","+","+```powershell","+powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File infra\\scripts\\stop-demo.ps1            # all of it","+powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File infra\\scripts\\stop-demo.ps1 -KeepCollector","+```","+","+From a terminal instead of the dashboard: `uv run python infra/scripts/e2e.py heavy_user`","+injects, waits, approves and prints the timeline.","+","+## Layout","+","+| Path | What it is |","+|---|---|","+| `packages/core` | Shared schemas, settings, database helpers, migrations |","+| `packages/agent` | The Pydantic AI agent on Gemma, the rule-based detector, the scenario injector |","+| `packages/fixes` | Fix templates' validation, rendering, CHR dry run, apply and rollback |","+| `templates/routeros` | The four fix templates (YAML) |","+| `services/worker` | Temporal workflows and activities, Sentry tracing |","+| `services/api` | FastAPI: REST, server-sent events, approvals, and the dashboard at `/` |","+| `services/collector` | Live pings and DNS timings from a real connection |","+| `infra/chr` | The MikroTik CHR test router in QEMU, and the template test harness |","+| `packages/detector`, `simgen`, `runbook`, `notify`, `eval`, `data` | The partner's experimental TabPFN detector, simulator, docs search and news check; not used by the running system |","+","+Tests: `uv sync --all-packages`, then `uv run pytest -m \"not live\"` and `uv run ruff check .`","+","+MIT licence."]}],"originalFile":"## HI","userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e849dbdc-c60f-418b-b714-1e4758606c79","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\hp\\NetCortex","sessionId":"88958964-2992-40b7-a2b1-a4d7674680fc","version":"2.1.301","gitBranch":"a/cleanup","slug":"wiggly-plotting-biscuit"}
